/**
 * The privacy policy document.
 *
 * SchoolCore ships as one Play build per school (`com.centit.rolpasunlight.app`,
 * `com.centit.divineacademy.app`, …), and Google Play wants each listing to point
 * at a policy that names *that* app. So the reviewed document is kept here as a
 * template with two holes in it — the app's name and the paragraph describing what
 * it does — and `/privacy_policy?schoolid=<id>` fills them from the school's app
 * listing.
 *
 * Three mentions deliberately do NOT move: the web application at nirsabi.com, the
 * product name behind it, and the shared back end are SchoolCore whichever build
 * you downloaded, and renaming those after a school would make the policy describe
 * a website that does not exist. They fill from `{{PRODUCT_NAME}}` instead.
 *
 * The wording is otherwise untouched, deliberately: it is the text Play reviewed,
 * and rewording it is a listing risk with no upside. Calling `buildPrivacyPolicy()`
 * with no arguments reproduces that document byte for byte, so the plain
 * `/privacy_policy` URL still serves exactly what it served before.
 */

const DEFAULT_APP_NAME = "SchoolCore";

const DEFAULT_APP_DESCRIPTION = `SchoolCore is a comprehensive school management system designed to streamline the operations of educational institutions. Our software facilitates robust management of student and staff enrollment, student billing, staff payroll, and accounting processes. With features such as exams management, entry-cards, marks entry, and result tabulation, SchoolCore ensures academic activities are efficiently handled. Additionally, our platform generates detailed reports and statistics, enhancing the decision-making process for school administrators. We also provide dedicated mobile applications for guardians and students, promoting transparency and ease of access to educational information. At SchoolCore, safeguarding the privacy of our users is paramount. We employ advanced security measures to protect personal data and adhere to stringent data protection standards to ensure the confidentiality and integrity of user information.`;

